    <verbatim|/private/tmp/ym-existence-20261111>.

    <item>Initial SHA-256: <verbatim|manuscript/existence/statement.tex>:
    <verbatim|0e0c686c89b67b6a5d98c51c7d0d934517c9001c6975f34886a86aba81062ac7>.

    <item>Initial SHA-256: <verbatim|manuscript/existence/reflection.tex>:
    <verbatim|5d3cfe90c7ad2221fa1592da9c5369935ae55cd0316fae9af62c3300ba92e503>.

    <item>Outcome: the Euclidean Hilbert-space/semigroup argument is valid
    conditional on its explicitly displayed correlation hypotheses. Several
    small statement corrections are requested for exact public
    correspondence. The existence of correlations satisfying those hypotheses
    and the passage to the relativistic endpoint remain outstanding; they are
    not established by this local argument.
  </itemize-minus>

  <section|Required statement corrections><label|required-statement-corrections>

  <\enumerate>
    <item>At <verbatim|ex-statement>, initial lines 24\U25, specify that both
    integer sequences are <strong|strictly> increasing.
    <verbatim|YangMills.WilsonFamily.periodStrict> and
    <verbatim|.denominatorStrict> in <verbatim|Lean/PublicWilson.lean> assert
    <verbatim|StrictMono>. Mere nondecrease would not imply diverging volume
    and vanishing mesh.

    <item>At initial lines 55\U58, say that the grade-space maps into the
    common label space are complex-linear injections.
    <verbatim|Hierarchy.toLabel> is a complex-linear map;
    <verbatim|Reconstructed.injective> supplies injectivity. \PMap
    injectively\Q omits linearity.

    <item>At <verbatim|ex-reconstructed>, initial lines 77\U80, state that
    the field is complex-linear separately in the label, the test, and the
    domain vector. <verbatim|FieldSystem.field> in
    <verbatim|Lean/PublicTheory.lean> is three nested linear maps. The
    current phrase \Pcomplex-linear fields Phi(A,f):D-\<gtr\>D\Q directly
    states only linearity in the domain vector.

    <item>At initial line 93, add that at least one label and test give a
    nonzero field operator. Faithfulness says every nonzero label is seen; it
    alone permits a zero label space. The public reconstruction explicitly
    includes the separate <verbatim|Hierarchy.Reconstructed.acts> clause in
    <verbatim|Lean/ChallengeSpec.lean>. A later trace conclusion might imply
    nontriviality with additional reasoning, but the definition should
    preserve the explicit endpoint condition rather than rely on an unproved
    implication.
  </enumerate>

  The endpoint's order of choices, separation of selected and mixed
  correlations, full-mesh fixed-row limits, subsequent volume refinement, and
  restricted time-analytic boundary interface are otherwise faithfully
  represented in the reviewed statement. Its deferred OPE and trace
  definitions were not present in the initial two-file review and require
  separate checking when supplied.

  <section|Euclidean Hilbert-space argument><label|euclidean-hilbert-space-argument>

  The following checks found no substantive gap in the conditional proof.

  <block|<tformat|<twith|table-width|1par>|<twith|table-hmode|exact>|<cwith|1|-1|1|-1|cell-hyphen|t>|<cwith|1|1|1|-1|cell-bborder|1ln>|<cwith|1|1|1|-1|cell-valign|bottom>|<table|<row|<cell|<strong|Manuscript
  step>>|<cell|<strong|Mathematical check>>|<cell|<strong|Source
  correspondence>>>|<row|<cell|Reflection and positive kernel>|<cell|Positive
  words have distinct points internally; reflected and unreflected parts lie
  in opposite strict half-spaces, so cross coincidences cannot occur.
  Reflection reverses concatenation and squares to the identity. Applying the
  reflection identity to <verbatim|(theta v)w> yields Hermitian symmetry. The
  displayed positivity assumption gives a positive semidefinite kernel on all
  positive words, including the empty word.>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.OS.reflect_twice>,
  <verbatim|twice_expect>, <verbatim|nonnegative> in
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/OS/Schwinger.lean>; <verbatim|YM.Table.Hierarchy.positive>
  in <verbatim|Lean/YM/Euclid/Words.lean>>>|<row|<cell|Separated bound
  implies cap>|<cell|Within-word sup distances are fixed. A cross-pair time
  difference is the sum of two positive original times and the nonnegative
  translation time. A single positive rho works for all finitely many pairs
  and all half-space translations. Empty and one-point configurations are
  correctly covered by the no-pairs case. Smoothness composed with the
  continuous configuration map gives relative continuity on the closed
  half-space.>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.OS.uniformAway>, <verbatim|correl> in
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/OS/Caps.lean>; derivative-order-zero case of
  <verbatim|YM.Table.Capped> in <verbatim|Lean/YM/Euclid/Table.lean>>>|<row|<cell|Cauchy\USchwarz
  and null quotient>|<cell|The finite sums define a Hermitian positive
  semidefinite sesquilinear form, conjugate-linear in its first variable.
  Minimizing the quadratic in the nonzero-diagonal case, and scaling a
  complex parameter in the zero-diagonal case, prove Cauchy\USchwarz. Thus a
  null vector pairs to zero with every vector; sums and scalar multiples of
  null vectors are null. The induced quotient form is well-defined and
  positive definite. Completion gives the asserted dense word
  span.>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Kernel.core>, <verbatim|host> in
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/Hilbert/Kolmogorov.lean>; the source uses separated
  completion of a seminormed space rather than spelling out the intermediate
  quotient. These are equivalent constructions.>>|<row|<cell|Uniform time
  bound>|<cell|Cap boundedness for the repeated word controls its translated
  norm squared. For finitely many words, the triangle inequality supplies a
  bound depending on that finite linear combination. No bound uniform over
  all words, labels or arities is claimed or
  needed.>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.OS.enough> in
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/OS/Flow.lean>>>|<row|<cell|Contraction before
  descent>|<cell|Defining translated vectors on formal sums avoids assuming
  null-space invariance. The translation identity yields <verbatim|norm(T_s
  c)^2 = \<less\>T_0 c,T_{2s} c\<gtr\>>. Cauchy\USchwarz bounds this by a
  times the finite supremum M. Since the norms are nonnegative and bounded,
  the supremum of their squares is M squared. Thus M squared \<less\>= aM,
  hence M \<less\>= a, including M=0. This proves descent without
  circularity.>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.OS.symmetrical>, <verbatim|contract> in
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/OS/Flow.lean>; <verbatim|YM.Kernel.Gram.by_bound> in
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/Hilbert/Kolmogorov.lean>>>|<row|<cell|Semigroup and
  symmetry>|<cell|Time translations preserve positive words; their
  composition law descends and extends by density. Setting one time parameter
  to zero gives symmetry on the dense span; boundedness extends it to the
  whole Hilbert space. An everywhere-defined bounded symmetric operator is
  self-adjoint.>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.OS.sym_time>, <verbatim|advances>;
  <verbatim|YM.OS.implement> in <verbatim|Lean/YM/OS/Dynamics.lean>>>|<row|<cell|Spatial
  unitary group>|<cell|Spatial shifts preserve positive words and commute
  with reflection. Translation invariance preserves all Gram pairings, so
  formal shifts preserve norms and descend. The inverse spatial shift proves
  surjectivity and unitarity. Commutation with time translations is verified
  on words and extends by density.>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.OS.sym_space>,
  <verbatim|parallel>, <verbatim|switch>; <verbatim|YM.OS.safe>,
  <verbatim|implement>>>|<row|<cell|Strong continuity>|<cell|For time
  translations the squared difference norm is expressed through the
  cap-continuous correlation at 2s, 2t and s+t. For spatial translations,
  diagonal terms are constant and the cross term is cap-continuous with the
  first shifted word held fixed; all spatial differences have zero time
  component. Finite sums are continuous. Approximation by a finite sum and
  the uniform operator bound 1 gives continuity for every vector. No
  operator-norm continuity is assumed.>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.OS.ketC>,
  <verbatim|contE>, <verbatim|contU>, <verbatim|implement> in
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/OS/Dynamics.lean>; <verbatim|YM.OS.strong> in
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/OS/Flow.lean>>>>>>

  Two notation corrections would make the proof cleaner without changing it:

  <\itemize-minus>
    <item>At <verbatim|ex-time-symmetry>, initial line 95, replace
    \PBilinearity\Q with \PSesquilinearity.\Q

    <item>In <verbatim|ex-contraction>, initial line 110, write the absolute
    value of the complex inner product before applying Cauchy\USchwarz. Its
    equality to the nonnegative norm square already ensures the current
    expression has a real value; the modulus makes that fact explicit and
    avoids ordering a visibly complex expression.
  </itemize-minus>

  The cap lemma is an accurate consequence of the source's stronger
  derivative estimates. It does not establish those estimates. In particular
  <verbatim|Table.Capped> permits constants depending on every fixed arity,
  label tuple and derivative order, and imposes no arity-growth control. The
  draft correctly leaves the growth hypotheses of a classical reconstruction
  theorem unverified.

  <section|Reconstruction and literature boundary><label|reconstruction-and-literature-boundary>

  The final paragraph of <verbatim|reflection.tex> correctly limits the
  proved result to Euclidean Hilbert-space dynamics. The hypotheses used here
  do not establish a selected pure phase, a unique invariant vacuum, local
  relativistic fields or a full analytic reconstruction. An internal
  <verbatim|Spec.Final> already packages these data and therefore cannot be
  treated as the result of this semigroup lemma alone.

  The original Osterwalder\USchrader paper is linked at
  <hlink|https://projecteuclid.org/journals/communications-in-mathematical-physics/volume-42/issue-3/Axioms-for-Euclidean-Greens-functions-II-with-an-Appendix-by/cmp/1103899050.pdf|https://projecteuclid.org/journals/communications-in-mathematical-physics/volume-42/issue-3/Axioms-for-Euclidean-Greens-functions-II-with-an-Appendix-by/cmp/1103899050.pdf>.
  The parent reports inspecting section IV.1. This reviewer attempted to open
  that exact URL with the web tool; it returned an anti-bot iframe and the
  iframe fetch failed. Consequently this report does not independently
  certify the paper's detailed hypotheses or its applicability. The draft
  presently uses it only as an expressly outstanding possible route, which is
  consistent with this evidence boundary. Its bibliographic record was not
  part of the two reviewed files.

