  <section|Final local supplement: extraction corrections and padded scalar
  age><label|final-local-supplement-extraction-corrections-and-padded-scalar-age>

  Re-read the final integrated extraction text in the parent's isolated
  clone. All seven initial extraction findings are resolved in this version.
  The proof now uses unsmeared lattice moments, the distinct
  Cyclic/NoHit/Gen/Conf domains, rounded functions with asymptotic
  equicontinuity, countable basis signatures and finite multilinear
  expansion, and the stronger compact bounds needed for smearing. The inner
  dominated-convergence proof supplies a constant times the indicator of the
  entire bounded fundamental box; outside the closed test support the sampled
  density eventually vanishes. The outer argument uses a compact neighborhood
  inside Conf and restricts the point convergence to the full-measure generic
  set. Before outer extraction the correct index is J_{f_per(k)}, not
  J_{rho_k}: the subsequence u defining rho has not yet been chosen. The
  integrated text respects this dependency. A fixed generic compact
  neighborhood belongs to the cyclic patch for every sufficiently large
  period, so the mesh-limit passage has a common domain.

  The Euclidean-property proposition now explicitly assumes a smooth
  extension on Conf agreeing with the generic limit and an exact finite
  pairing representation with index-independent coefficients. These are
  substantive additional hypotheses, not conclusions of compactness. Under
  those hypotheses its finite-sum reflection-positivity passage is valid; the
  separately reviewed bump argument then gives point positivity, including
  diagonal entries with spatial ties. No remaining substantive defect was
  identified in this conditional extraction argument. This does not verify
  that the constructed Wilson trajectory meets the hypotheses.

  The final scalar recurrence includes the nonnegative offset Z in
  y_j=R+Z+\|t_j-s\|. Rechecking the proof shows all inequalities remain valid
  because y_j\<gtr\>=R, and C,R,q,mu are independent of Z and s. This
  resolves the previous missing-offset observation. The text remains a
  finite-interval scalar variant with an explicit terminal estimate; its
  required RG majorants and their parameter uniformity remain unproved here.
  The declaration is YM.RG08.Rate.Stair.fade_solve in Rate/Ascent.lean.

  The current statement differs from the last reviewed version by a
  background-prerequisites paragraph only; this does not change its
  mathematical content. The other previously checked files retain their
