  <section|Individual reflection and orthogonal
  covariance><label|individual-reflection-and-orthogonal-covariance>

  Reviewed parent reflection-transport.tex after the generic-grid qualifier,
  SHA-256 <verbatim|f7746c679729c2867b8fb1124e3607883491fbb5a49e1b186aa4c3020077e1c8>.
  Read actual Phase/Approx.lean and Square.lean and Work/B04.lean, B05.lean,
  B06.lean. No remaining substantive local defect was identified in this
  conditional proof.

  The random-variable lemma retains the essential order: for fixed
  approximation index k and number m of simultaneous copies, remove the
  ordered cutoff for sufficiently large t, then t tends to infinity, then m
  tends to infinity, and only then k. The bound R_k need not be uniform in k.
  The error is uniform over copy pairs, and finitely many eventualities can
  be intersected at fixed m. Positive translation directions separate
  different copies in every coordinate. The original wording omitted internal
  genericity, which translations cannot create; the final text correctly
  restricts this stage to internally generic grid words and later uses norm
  continuity on all distinct configurations.

  For real basis labels, reflected conjugation agrees with ordinary
  reflection up to word reversal, so D*=\<minus\>D. Nonnegative
  ordinary-square limiting expectation is therefore \<minus\>\|\|D
  Omega\|\|\<twosuperior\>, forcing D Omega=0. Separating vacuum gives D=0.
  Density extends positions, then genuine complex multilinearity extends
  basis labels. The null-label test gives zero slab operator by dense
  two-sided matrix elements, justifying quotient independence and the stated
  signed-action compatibility.

  The alternate common-forward direction b=e_time+K^{-1}e_time is valid
  whenever a=(K e_time)_time\<gtr\>\<minus\>1; both time components equal
  1+a. If a=\<minus\>1, prepend the ordinary time reflection. This is a
  shorter valid variant of B06's three cases. Simultaneous pair invariance,
  applied backward then forward around individual reflection of the second
  word, gives each conjugate hyperplane reflection. Adjoint left tests and
  cyclic density separate the resulting vectors, and the separating vacuum
  upgrades equality to operators. The elementary dimension induction proves
  that these reflections generate O(4), respecting the quotient group action.
  Ordinary conjugation and transport of coordinate-axis positivity then
  follow with the stated raw signed compatibility.

  The bounded real approximants on the arbitrarily fine admitted grids are
  still assumed, not constructed. Ordinary probability positivity alone does
  not supply them. The report does not certify that upstream quantitative
  input. Commands actually run include targeted source reads, final shasum,
  and git diff --check (passed); no Lean or LaTeX build or blueprint checker
  was run for this supplement.

  <section|Boundary words, fields, and group
  action><label|boundary-words-fields-and-group-action>

  Reviewed parent reconstruction.tex, SHA-256
