  continuity) and Motion.lean (embedding and group action). No substantive
  local defect was identified in this conditional theorem.

  The two independent heat parameters correctly control all four terms in the
  norm difference, including diagonal and reversed pairs, giving a genuine
  norm limit in the complete Euclidean Hilbert space. The resulting Gram
  formula supplies positivity. The null quotient is preserved by each left
  concatenation because its adjoint-word identity moves the concatenation to
  the other argument; this is the essential source <verbatim|compactor> step.
  Matrix elements then establish bilinearity without prematurely imposing
  formal word relations. Joint Schwartz-test Gram continuity gives strong
  continuity of each field on each fixed domain vector. The adjoint inclusion
  and closability follow on the one dense common domain; self-adjointness is
  neither asserted nor needed here.

  Locality is exactly the stated adjacent insertion identity with arbitrary
  exterior words; faithfulness is separately assumed and used without
  strengthening. Gram-preserving word action yields the unitary
  representation, and continuity of its matrix coefficients yields strong
  continuity by the norm-square identity and dense approximation. The map of
  word vectors to cold Euclidean vectors is an isometry, not claimed onto;
  eventual translation intertwining passes through the norm limit. Spectral
  support and unique vacuum are correctly excluded from the conclusion
  pending the additional Euclidean translation facts. Actual analytic
  boundary values, Lorentz/locality/detection properties, and the
  independent-height limit remain substantive hypotheses until their separate
  producer chapters are completed.

  The exact <verbatim|Small.heatCup>/<verbatim|Lamp> producer and the nearest
  analytic source chain are now recorded in the separate
