  <section|Analytic continuation and full ordered-height
  boundary><label|analytic-continuation-and-full-ordered-height-boundary>

  Reviewed parent analytic-boundary.tex after its explicit suffix-invariant
  addition and display correction, SHA-256
  <verbatim|f605215e4cd0e65cf8d18216948a616f4b0f6786a1fe42356f1d970415c030ef>.
  The actual source chain inspected for the preceding heated-word map is the
  basis for correspondence: C01--C04 and Shift/Ridge, Breath, Osc. No
  remaining substantive local defect was identified.

  Centered singleton insertions descend to the common union using the stated
  all-exterior null/inclusion compatibilities. The singleton AllCopy case
  gives the required labelwise power in p. Padding B_{p+u}=E_u B_p E_u and
  the corresponding leg identity prove scalar product independence of width;
  strict inequalities permit one width locally, which proves holomorphy and
  spatial continuity. The source only has strong continuity of spatial
  translations, and the manuscript correctly uses it at successive varying
  vectors rather than assuming operator-norm continuity. The added
  imaginary-time suffix invariant has positions (x_i-X,y_i-Y-p), with
  positive heat duration y_first-Y-2p. The final complete word shift is
  (-x_1,-y_1+p), and vacuum translation invariance gives the scalar Euclidean
  identification.

  Taking p=k/8 yields the uniform real-position bound C k^{-m}. This supplies
  fixed-height integrability and continuity. A uniform complex disc gives a
  Cauchy derivative bound; compact cutoff integration by parts is justified
  by the bounded real-time derivative and Schwartz L1 bounds, and produces
  the correct minus-i test derivative. The exact finite Taylor sum has
  derivative (-s)^m/m! times the next tested derivative. Its remainder is
  uniformly integrable over s in (0,1] because the gap power s^{-m} is
  canceled by s^m. Dominated convergence extends it to the closed weakly
  ordered height cone, with a finite continuous Schwartz-seminorm bound.
  Uniqueness of the interior limit passes test linearity and label
  multilinearity despite label-dependent power exponents. Arity zero and one
  have vacuous ordering requirements and are covered.

  This chapter now supplies a substantial analytic producer previously left
  as an opaque boundary assumption. The complex heat extension itself remains
  explicit input, as do the earlier union/inclusion and slab estimates. The
  conclusion alone does not give Lorentz covariance, locality or label
  faithfulness. Only targeted source/manuscript reads and a final hash were
  performed here; no build or blueprint checker was run by this reviewer.

  <section|Independent heat-vector bridge><label|independent-heat-vector-bridge>

  Reviewed parent heat-vectors.tex, SHA-256
  <verbatim|31e865e455f9487d2d1c64c8fa361c799309b1e0ebf9d3c7dd6e539e2d27320e>,
  against the full C22--C24 source already inspected. No substantive
  mathematical or source-correspondence defect was found. The first heat leg
  subtracts p, each interior leg subtracts 2p, and the Euclidean recursion
  with a preceding half-width q0 has positions (x_i-X0,y_i-Y0-q0), exactly as
  in the source. The two words may have different admissible widths.

  The scalar continuation uses the first Hilbert vector at conjugate(c), so
  antilinearity restores holomorphy. Its negative/reversed first heights and
  reversed first real positions have the right signs: real times are not
  reflected. A single horizontal strip contains both the imaginary equality
  segment and c=1, permitting the ordinary one-variable identity theorem. The
  proof includes empty words.

  Fixed-height shots are continuous images of a separable finite-dimensional
  position space and therefore have separable range; the uniform-in-position
  norm bound times an L1 Schwartz test proves Bochner integrability without
  global Hilbert separability. Absolute product bounds justify Fubini.
  Reversing the first coordinates is volume preserving and produces the
  conjugated/reversed first tests. The combined heights (-ns,...,-s,t,...,mt)
  are ordered for every independent positive s,t and tend to zero in the full
  ordered cone, so the previously proved full-height boundary theorem
  supplies the Gram limit. Translation by X+a gives the same sign as tests
  f(.\<minus\>a), and the bounded translation operator passes through the
  Bochner integral.

  Unitary imaginary-axis heat boundary values and their composition with the
  interior extension are explicitly assumed for this last translation step.
  They remain the next spectral-analysis producer, rather than being silently
  deduced from operator-norm holomorphy alone. No Lean or LaTeX build or
  blueprint checker was run by this reviewer.

  <section|Complex heat extension and unique
  vacuum><label|complex-heat-extension-and-unique-vacuum>

  Reviewed parent complex-heat.tex after the spatial-vacuum hypothesis was
  added, SHA-256 <verbatim|383d05e68932671dca47c1a8aeefa0f3ad598c3e68975401f3cce6e62cd348fe>.
  Read full Heat/Rows.lean, Extend.lean and Imaginary.lean. Continuous
  functional calculus uses the previously independently inspected Williams
  Theorem 2.19. No remaining substantive defect was found.

  The scalar functions lambda^z for Re(z)\<gtr\>0 extend continuously by zero
  at spectral zero. Uniform bounds for lambda^delta times powers of
  log(lambda) give the stated uniform Taylor remainder and therefore
  operator-norm holomorphy. Positive rational roots of E_1 are identified by
  applying functional calculus first to E_{1/n}; strong continuity then
  identifies every positive real time. The repeated-halving proof of
  injectivity is correct and is an elementary variant of the source's
  analytic uniqueness argument. Self-adjointness gives dense range. The norm
  identity for E(1\<minus\>it) permits extension from ran(E_1), and testing
  bounded compositions on that dense range gives the edge law, group law,
  unitarity and commutation. Strong boundary convergence uses
  E_epsilon\<rightarrow\>I strongly, not in operator norm.

  The original spatial paragraph assumed only a commuting unitary
  representation. This was insufficient for the claimed full translation
  fixed space: E_t=I on C and nontrivial scalar spatial phases give a
  counterexample. The final text explicitly requires spatial invariance of
  Omega_E, a property already available for the actual Euclidean vacuum. With
  that hypothesis, holomorphic constancy proves time-fixed equals heat-fixed,
  and the selected one-dimensional heat ground plus the isometric intertwiner
  proves unique invariant vacuum in the reconstructed Hilbert space. No mass
  gap follows or is claimed.

  This chapter discharges the complex heat and imaginary-axis translation
  inputs left explicit in the analytic-boundary and heat-vectors snapshots
  above. The full forward-cone spectral measure remains a distinct
  obligation; the unique-vacuum argument does not supply it. No Lean or LaTeX
  build or blueprint checker was run by this reviewer.

  <section|Fourier half-space support and conditional cone
  improvement><label|fourier-half-space-support-and-conditional-cone-improvement>

  Reviewed parent fourier-support.tex after the Lorentz-group precision edit,
  SHA-256 <verbatim|7da33ddfdb0ce8533441e935c566a56cd251ac4bd701f1c39d20da6869f8bf12>.
  Read actual Work/C05.lean, C06.lean, Shift/Closing.lean and the group
  definition in Mink/Lorentz.lean. No remaining substantive local defect was
