  <section|Free-kernel pair: corrections required><label|free-kernel-pair-corrections-required>

  Reviewed lattice-drafter free-kernel-estimates.tex
  <verbatim|47fcc9d52354564e5c3aab55f10ac98189c65481cc1718d57ad7e0323bac4357>
  and free-kernel-components.tex <verbatim|155ba8d2622b0ae01629956ebf28fe0fbd6f42be9e17c26e3e18a97755014e2f>.
  Neither is accepted in this snapshot. Read actual Train, Reserve, Bend,
  Feed, Lines, Buffer, Strands, Cable, Moderate, and relevant
  Signal/Portions/Wire definitions. The contour-shift coefficient estimate,
  alias weight summation, reciprocal-overlap permutation and centered carry
  phase are sound. The branch formulas and component proof need the
  corrections sent to the drafter.

  Flux must reverse momentum before transpose; the displayed plus-q flux does
  not equal Signal.flux. The land divisor takes the side P.land.mass, not the
  mass-filter function. Signal is wedge multiplication by a one-form, with
  grade weight independent of the degree; the claimed degree-r product bound
  is false at r=0. The reciprocal mass in the latch needs a positive
  principal lower bound, not its upper estimate. Train stage orientation must
  be corrected and bare patch mass filters distinguished from cumulative
  train smooth filters. Declare the sup norm in the quantitative
  cube-shrinking step, or adjust dimensional constants. The alias C_eta
  should include both real and imaginary margins.

  The component exposition also lacks definitions of several crucial
  elementary and recursive functions. In particular the coefficient-one
  principal-plank lower bound and its geometric-mass induction are
  substantive: multiplying a fixed lower constant at every hop would fail for
  unbounded histories. The feed estimate must use f=1 and retain its inverse
  mass squared weight until summing the explicitly defined nozzle list. The
  port lower bound must select a maximizing lift coordinate. The bend upper
  bound requires its actual formula with reciprocal halo, lid, and bulb
  controls before the bend reciprocal is taken. These are exposition
  gaps/source mismatches, not evidence of false source theorems. The closing
  unconditional component proposition cannot be counted as proved while the
  final remark leaves its essential induction open. No source edits or builds
  were made.

  <section|Trace normalization and all-radius
  limit><label|trace-normalization-and-all-radius-limit>

  Reviewed parent trace-asymptotic.tex, SHA-256
  <verbatim|ea67b21fa62625532697710fd0ca52bc36facb76deedfae2a2508c9d60bd82d6>,
  against full TraceExtension/Foundation/Constant, Chart/Masts, North,
  Nectar, Time, and Verse/Pears, Round, Day, Cape. No substantive local
  mathematical or main-step correspondence defect was found. The orthogonal
  reflection matrix curvature contraction gives 24 for ordered pairs, and the
  two cross-Wick pairings with the factor (1/4)^2 give exactly 3 dim(g)/(pi^4
  \|x\|^8). Identification with the actual reference hierarchy remains
  explicitly required.

  The rank comparison yields a one-dimensional conserved space. The same
  nonzero Ward flux limit for physical and trial tensors forces their real
  proportionality constants to tend to one, exactly North.year_spec.
  Multiplying their inverses into the separately controlled trace limits is
  legitimate. The centered unit shift vanishes with B_i r_i^4 and the
  eventual unit intertwining, as in Nectar.shift_unit/july. Finite-basis
  bilinearity proves moving-label convergence rather than assuming uniform
  convergence for arbitrary labels. The exact B_i^2 r_i^8 factor and squared
  logarithmic ratio cancel to 3 dim(g)/pi^4 using d2=-b0/2.

  The generic diagonal shots have Euclidean separation t; positivity of the
  specialized trace spectral measure gives monotonicity, which brackets the
  intended radius between rounded radii with fixed t below/above one. The
  bad-sequence subsequence contradiction then gives the full positive-radius
  limit, matching Verse.Cape. This retains the source's main route. Its
  explicit trace-comparison assumption still includes the scale selection,
  ultraviolet basis error, moving-label/stress data and specialized spectral
  measure; no production of those inputs is certified by this bounded review.
  Consequently this is a conditional local result and does not complete the
  existence proof. No build was run.

  <section|Specialized field and trace spectral
  measure><label|specialized-field-and-trace-spectral-measure>

  Reviewed parent trace-spectrum.tex, SHA-256
  <verbatim|2f2c16737f123073f07ec3e5132fd4c6df83ad8021d20fa44d2d32aaece494e7>.
  Read full Heat/Duration, Paley/Icon and Mapped, TraceExtension/Damping,
  PolynomialGrowth, Relative, Momentum, Centered and WilsonTrace; rechecked
  Heat/Lift's heat identification after its earlier full review. No
  substantive mathematical or main-step correspondence defect was found.

  The Gaussian uniqueness proof uses b=-2 epsilon s, whose horizontal phase
  cancels exactly and whose remaining nonzero constant is exp(-epsilon s
  squared). Gaussian rescaling then recovers the point value by dominated
  convergence. This applies to bounded continuous vector matrix coefficients,
  not distributional boundary values. Characteristic-function uniqueness
  yields the precise double-height damping. Width independence of the point
  vector follows by all four mixed Gram products; the common-width semigroup
  identity and comparison through s+1 give the same undamped measure at every
  positive height.

  The gap bound controls the entire energy sublevel set with constant
  exp(2)C. The dyadic shell estimate then gives an integrable rapid weight
  and permits the joint Schwartz boundary identity by dominated convergence.
  The plus Fourier convention and displacement x1-x0 agree with Relative and
  Momentum. Smeared field PVM masses are exactly \|f_+\| squared times this
  same measure; compact smooth Fourier weights equal to one on each ball
  yield both uniqueness and forward-cone support. The Lorentz pushforward
  uses the inverse transpose, and Euclidean trace invariance descends through
  the boost-generator relation to the Lorentz scalar. Centering removes the
  one-point boundary through actual holomorphic uniqueness.

  Rechecked the specialized-measure removal in parent trace-asymptotic.tex,
  SHA-256 <verbatim|5153c8ba36230fe0bd73a286477f4121d7461939501850b821fb7265e57f0a04>.
  For the reconstructed centered trace, its positive Laplace measure now
  follows from this chapter rather than a separate assumption. The
  ultraviolet/stress comparison and scale-selection inputs remain
  outstanding. This bounded review does not certify the full existence proof.
  Live issue26 comments were rechecked through the GitHub connector; claim
  unchanged through 2026-11-12 16:40 UTC, newest progress comment6803403446
  retains draft/conditional status. No builds or GitHub mutations were
  performed.

  <section|One OPE prescription across all
  degrees><label|one-ope-prescription-across-all-degrees>

  Reviewed parent ope-prescription.tex, SHA-256
  <verbatim|b332b2c3cd21bc6224659e9f1452b8c37a81a451e907f94728ab5ecdbdd4bd78>,
  against full OPE/Splitting/{Basis,Needle,Legacy,Detector}.lean. No
  substantive mathematical or main-step correspondence defect was found.
  Separation by physical exterior tests gives dual spanning in finite
  dimension. The corrected quotient lift F=S-RBS satisfies qF=I and BF=0,
  with the latter annihilating every old detector because b_alpha,n
  B=b_alpha,n+1. The exact decomposition v=Fqv+RBv establishes reconstruction
  and all four old/new biorthogonality cases. Freezing actual finite detector
  combinations as well as fields gives the all-degree prescription; the
  high-detector vanishing follows by lifting lower-degree reconstruction.

  The raw product coefficient uses only separated actual correlations and is
  zero elsewhere. Separation depends on positions only, so multilinearity
  survives this convention. Filtration compatibility, singleton
  reconstruction, simultaneous translations/permutations, and finite positive
  detector clearance are correctly accounted for. Empty spectator lists
  impose no clearance restriction, and orthogonal rotation preserves the
  needed radial clearance. This is the source's coherent prescription and raw
  detector step; rotational/reality averaging, homogeneous projection, and
  quantitative OPE error are not established by this chapter. No asymptotic
  OPE estimate is claimed.

  Checked parent assembly.tex, SHA-256 <verbatim|0dbc2ab862922fdea4455970a5771a53793b58021084fa27f7a8235e6f4b3d11>:
  removing finite-profile exclusion from the independent input is justified
