  Grouping fine observables by coarse cells preserves the product of prices.
  Distinct copied positions cannot share a fine cell, using aligned nested
  tilings and the stated separation. The replicated groups use the same
  margins, so the room inequalities charge the original arities, not the
  number of replicas. Period enlargement is taken before the fine cutoff at
  each fixed integer translation, and the long-translation limit follows
  afterward. Finite-basis expansion handles moving finite-dimensional labels
  along an arbitrary nontrivial refinement of the same ordered cutoff filter;
  separate iterated label limits are not assumed. Expanding the alternating
  conjugated products retains the operator order and yields (A* A)^m as in
  B17. Full support and arbitrarily high even moments bound every character,
  including measure-zero phases, and hence the Gelfand norm.

  Removing coordinate ties uses scalar continuity in each phase and then the
  norm characterization, not unsupported norm continuity of the
  algebra-valued correlation. The forbidden-residue construction clears both
  the fixed generic cluster and the origin, with a true common finer grid and
