  Inspected full MergeProof/Twigs, Ac/{Tree,Table},
  OPE/Grouping/{Replicate,Birth,Charge,Wiring,Care,Papyrus,Shift,Stator,Stained,Fibers,Sugary,Dew,Gush,Ebb,River},
  and Further/SHELL_BIRTH_49/Fusing/Coal. No remaining substantive local
  mathematical or main-step correspondence defect was found after the stated
  hypothesis/uniqueness corrections.

  The forest recursion uses an injective encoding of a finite
  connected-component selection by chosen roots and residual rooted packs.
  Its upper product may repeat labels, but this only adds nonnegative terms;
  the encoded terms themselves retain each label once with exact weight.
  Strong induction closes with the cover-cardinality inequality. Removing the
  empty pack gives exp(gamma)-1, and taking suprema over finite label
  families justifies the arbitrary-index nonnegative sum. No repeated-label
  logarithmic polymer expansion is asserted.

  Enlarging each support pays at most k per marked child, with the exact
  exponential cancellation. The marked 1/h reserve compensates all old
  locations within each group; representative occupancy remains bounded by
  the old occupancy because the selected old marks are distinct. Zero-mark
  entries pay no new-location reserve. The resulting majorant is exactly
  2(1+ell) eta (ell T exp(sigma)+A)+(1+ell)B. Healthy/unhealthy splitting is
  paid twice before taking coefficient suprema. Positive integer block/group
  bounds and nonnegative budget/weighted quantities are now explicit.

  The exact algebra uses the source's full squarefree marker algebra and
  complete-group linear reaping, not an incorrect global algebra-homomorphism
  claim. The two-stage graph first connects common group names and then
  exposes walls precisely on name-components containing dirty entries.
  Restriction and reconstruction of this graph justify uniqueness. Surviving
  old terms have complete groups in each component. A dirty ordinary
  component must attach to a selected flagged entry by the global flag
  inventory. The forward and reverse constructions preserve coefficients,
  old-label inventories, flag support disjointness and mark completeness. In
  the reverse direction a repeated unmarked label would lie in two hot
  supports, while a repeated marked label would repeat a group; both are
  excluded. Thus the component-set map is injective across ordinary and
  flagged kinds, as required by Papyrus.carries. The coefficient bounds apply
  to the actual reconstructed arrays without hidden flag or ordering
  multiplicity.

  A component with no marks is necessarily a single zero-mark flagged entry:
  no name edges occur, no support enlargement occurs, and its old flagged
  supports are disjoint. Hence every vacuum support coefficient is unchanged,
  not merely their total sum. Finite products and flag indicators preserve
  the stated local dependence, measurability and gauge invariance; covariance
  follows by the finite entry relabeling and component uniqueness. No
  smoothness across flag boundaries is claimed. The ordinary and flagged
  indexing families are now explicitly finite in the exact identity. The
  analytic singleton/local projection and RG descent estimates remain
  separate obligations; neither chapter treats finite algebra or counting as
  their proof. No source edits, builds or metadata approvals were made.

  <section|Selected-history centered construction: revised candidate still
