  <section|Singleton recovery and higher-term
  separation><label|singleton-recovery-and-higher-term-separation>

  Reviewed parent ope-singletons.tex, final SHA-256
  <verbatim|38f846d42a399c17f1b39394ed9ae0aa93d6d3a0e09d4cde656dd8ccdeab1f9e>,
  against full MergeProof/Dock, North/{Blade,Loon,Frost,Arbor,Verve,Anise},
  MergeProof/{Hens,Grant,Stretch}, and OPE/Replicas/Arbor at the source pin.
  No remaining substantive local mathematical or main-step correspondence
  defect was found after adding the explicit input covariance condition.

  Retaining just the singleton coefficient in the hit budget at its named
  origin gives a/w and b/w without a mark-count factor. Two real elementary
  insertions realize each complex local coefficient at cost twice its real
  bound. Concatenating their finite lists gives exactly 2a/w+2b/w, anchored
  at the same origin, with the scalar constant recorded separately. The
  dictionary slot and eligibility properties are explicitly assumed. A finite
  realization also yields a dominated countable index family; the summed
  flagged profiles are independent of auxiliary index choices.

  The decomposition by marker degree is exact. The unchanged higher
  coefficients retain their hit bounds and local properties. The linear
  density expansion sums absolutely: distinguished-index products are bounded
  by B_v times the product of 1+\|k_j^0\|, hence by B_v exp(B_0). This also
  justifies replacing finite pair-index sums by countable dictionary-index
  sums without hidden multiplicities; disjoint nonempty supports exclude
  duplicate pairs. Nonvanishing of the background density is used only for
  the stated uniqueness implication, not to establish the direct algebraic
  decomposition. This local direct separation is compatible with the source
  plume/plank route.

  The reserve w/8 gives 4/w=1/(2w'), and lowering positive marker weights
  decreases all higher coefficient prices. Covariance now explicitly assumes
  the input covariance inherited from regrouping; reindexing support sums
  proves it without equivariant dictionary choices. Dictionary production,
  background validity and the later local projection/transfer estimate remain
  explicit inputs or separate obligations. No builds, source edits or
  metadata approvals were made.

