  <section|One-scale local transport consumer><label|one-scale-local-transport-consumer>

  Reviewed parent local-transfer.tex, final SHA-256
  <verbatim|42ccf5ebb31aa2d9b9d189fb8db8257277906c2af5ae88b5807f854921970d97>,
  against full MergeProof/{Temper,Copse,Plaza,Cargo,Decaf,Castle,Dock,Fruit,Heap,Close,Garnish,Sigil,Vale,SpreadR,Click}
  and Extra/MULTISOURCE_BOUNDS/Root through root_hit. No remaining
  substantive local mathematical or main-step correspondence defect was found
  after the requested precision fixes.

  The anchored-to-site argument has the exact siteFactor exp(1)[2(16M+9)]^4
  and correctly counts all named sources through occupancy, including
  coincident anchors. Finite-slot compression of countable real/imaginary
  insertion families pays exactly twice the original cost, conditional on the
  stated quote continuity and local insertion properties. Higher-term
  insertion lists pay 4q. The heap expansion uses unweighted fares excluding
  the support exponential; multiplying the latter only once per same-slot
  product gives T+exp(T)T. Compatibility and nonempty marker sets make the
  squarefree exponential identity exact, and added products have no singleton
  component.

  The response closure is a nonzero-term bijection through support-connected
  components. Every response support meets a flag and hence an old flagged
  vertex; every flag in the union belongs to an old flagged vertex in that
  same component. Reverse reconstruction preserves inventories and cannot
  create cross-component overlaps. Vacuum components are single old flagged
  vertices; one response vertex gives exactly the stated star of mutually
  disjoint background supports, and two responses cannot contribute a
  singleton. Absolute summability justifies the countable background-index
  realization. The forest bound gives exp(A)-1 at the stated reserve, with no
  output-pair multiplicity loss.

  The final weight inequality converts exponent t+eta into t with precisely
  factor a_*. Duty specialization dI, T=N S_R d+4d and A=u+N S_E d matches
  Temper.Duty.pre and its half-unit reserve. Fine-prior and transition-slice
  integrability are now explicit, as required before pulling a polynomial
  factor through integration. Nonvanishing of the coarse density is used only
  to identify the prescribed ordinary singleton. The analytic
  finite-insertion estimate (Volant.reserves), quote construction and
  singleton transition expansions remain explicit obligations. This is a
  local consumer pass, not a proof of those analytic suppliers. No builds,
  source edits or metadata approvals were made.

