  respects in North/{Angled,Morsel}, and the Graces/Aspire host and coinFee
  definitions. No remaining substantive local mathematical or main-step
  correspondence defect was found after explicitly requiring positive kappa
  and a separate raw marked-profile identity.

  The principal reserve pays the polynomial derivative cost by exp(D/2),
  leaving the stated half-unit decay on large support. Combining two real
  insertions uses common supports, principal index and majorants;
  zero-padding preserves density and cost. The complex scaling costs twice
  the scalar modulus and the raw seed remains zero. The local splitting
  bounds total regular mass by twice e0, coefficient change by F_d times that
  mass, and normalized forced mass by b0 plus the same splitting charge. The
  host 1+2F_d(1+C_orb+C_turn) pays both the orbit coefficient norm and the
  transported remainder norm. This agrees with the actual source's larger
  motion-dependent allowance, rather than only the unturned splitting cost.
  The zero imaginary insertion may retain the real insertion's majorant,
  giving the source's available fine cost 2m.

  The density identity alone does not determine the marked profile. The final
  text correctly assumes that profile identity separately, then adds the
  exact splitting hook with its proved response price. Thus the final
  elementary projection and transition bounds follow conditionally on the
  localized raw expansion, its tail and forced estimates, singleton identity,
  and same-history smallness inequalities. Those analytic producers remain
  open inputs here. No builds, source edits or metadata approvals were made.

  <section|Differentiating the tilted block
  expansion><label|differentiating-the-tilted-block-expansion>

  Reviewed parent leaf-expansion.tex at SHA-256
  <verbatim|22ed8bcc327a5892904b94332ca64dda7c8e3be57221e05c1d937686a9181e7b>.
  Inspected Mallow/Tonic and Fresh in full, the normalization and derivative
  identities in Brisk/Drip, Daisy/Coasts and Corral, the tail consumer in
  Sparks, and the Rate definition in Numerics. No remaining substantive local
  mathematical or main-step correspondence defect was found after adding the
  ungrouped pointed absolute bound and removing the incorrect claim that the
  earlier pointed rebate proof supplied the two whole-gas exponential
  regroupings.

  Joint value-plus-derivative witnesses multiply without a degree factor. The
  mean-value theorem and counting-measure dominated convergence justify
  differentiating countable sums without continuity of each derivative. On a
  finite lattice, nonempty-support hit bounds give summability of activity
  prices. Expanding the product of witness sums also bounds the full sum of
  absolute pointed derivatives by D times the product price, so the source
  marked gas is obtained on the original addresses without relying on
  cancellation within each finite family. Differentiating locality, gauge and
  flag equalities preserves format; measurable difference quotients and the
  anchored hit bound give the exact D s forced cost, including D=0.

  The logarithmic derivative and the two expressly assumed fusion identities
  yield the exact a(theta)/a(0) normalization and hence the full
  coarse-density multiplier. The polynomial reserve is now the actual
  inverse-reserve-power times factorial times exp(reserve) constant, proved
  directly from the exponential series. Positive-order cluster tails and
  order-zero nonprincipal molecules are charged separately; the latter use
  excess cardinality at least one and an injective indexing map. Insertion
  debt retains its fine support exponential and inverse gain. The stated
  source rate exponents give tail exponent q/2 and the strict q/4 payment.

  The tilted expansion, its two fusion identities and numerical majorants,
  mixed/connected input estimates and their rate production, and the
  independent singleton-profile identity remain explicit hypotheses. This
  local pass validates the differentiation and downstream arithmetic, not the
  complete nonlinear expansion producer. No builds, source edits or metadata
  approvals were made.

  <section|Repeated-label connected clusters and the real
  logarithm><label|repeated-label-connected-clusters-and-the-real-logarithm>

  Reviewed parent cluster-expansion.tex at SHA-256
  <verbatim|7cef87fd1c751b3685669c32bccac1cc16d7dcda44f7ff2f34cae8696d21dad9>.
  Inspected the exact definitions and relevant bodies in
  Push/ABSOLUTE_SUMS/{Graph,Parent,Weigh,Forest,Clusters,Ursell,Coef,Gas,FiniteLog,Log},
  including the Breadth interface used by Graph. No substantive local
  mathematical or main-step correspondence defect was found.

  The breadth-first least-parent construction partitions connected subgraphs
  into Boolean intervals with the stated level and order restrictions.
  Alternating cancellation pays at most one per tree. The normalized overlap
  kernel has row mass at most one; leaf elimination pays any rooted tree. The
  max(delta cover,1) fan factor and exponential reserve cancel at every
  internal vertex. Summing child factorials over all parent maps gives
  exactly m! binomial(2m,m), hence at most m! 4^m. The subsequent root
  averaging has the source's m! versus (m+1)! normalization, and connected
  support unions give the actual cover-weighted local tail. Repeated activity
  labels are retained throughout.

  For signed activities, reflexivity removes repeated-label tuples in the
  all-graph gas coefficient. Splitting off the component containing the
  distinguished occurrence gives the exact factorial recurrence. Absolute
  derivative convergence on an interval containing [0,1] permits the real
  differential equation P'=L'P; its normalized constant solution establishes
  positivity and the real logarithm without assuming either. Finite-alphabet
  exhaustion is justified by the uniform absolute majorants, including for
  arbitrary alphabets after restriction to nonzero activity support. This
  discharges the combinatorial cluster-tail and logarithm identities from the
  displayed vertex hit/smallness condition. Producing actual nonlinear
  activities and those vertex estimates remains an analytic input. No builds,
  source edits or metadata approvals were made.

