  <section|Selected-history centered bound, final conditional
  snapshot><label|selected-history-centered-bound-final-conditional-snapshot>

  Final local reread passed limits-author centered-construction.tex SHA-256
  <verbatim|0686cb230b2de4c9a12e6c8391dec333490d6448247da7e06e0415977e606bec>,
  evidence <verbatim|9b47ad1ff972e7a382b4de8c93b7c0f9ff330742f9d1ef59c4e221445b6a56b3>.
  This is a conditional local pass. The finite-menu nonlinear response and
  uniform selected-history receipt production are explicit inputs; the draft
  no longer relies on the unpassed lattice supplier candidate. Its
  coefficient interface is restricted to quiet and specified singleton
  coefficients for each box. The earlier report's pending geometric/scale
  corrections are resolved.

  The squarefree census estimate counts active supports by a contained named
  origin and pays both ordinary and flagged support arrays. The finite pass
  and admissible field product yield the exact scalar/action bill. Closed
  Haar balls and an ambient packing bound give the stated positive
  denominator on the calm event; the normalized product prior has four
  independent edge variables per lattice site. Absolute integrability and
  finite-dimensional coefficient extraction justify each backwards
  transition. General allowances (3 fly, fly) produce the +6 bill, distinct
  from the matched-reference +5 variant. Full-census root extraction is then
  elementary and preserves all period/label/site uniformities.

  For the geometric step, the actual cover requires connected halo union. Its
  center graph has edges whenever halos meet or touch across one max-distance
  step. Spanning-tree out-and-back paths may use intermediate sites and
  advance coordinates simultaneously; their length is at most D(4B+2).
  Separated named origins force time gaps B^2-2B, giving B\|I\|\<less\>=64D
  for \|I\|\<gtr\>=2 and B\<gtr\>=8. The mint inequality has the correct
  orientation: old marched weight is at most delta times new weight times
  exp(B/128), hence multi-marker products lose only half a covering exponent.
  Both adjacent site families retain occupancy at most r_i. The response
  shrinkage is exactly d_i=delta_i.

  The coefficient-bond induction uses the actual dilation, column and
  Cherry/Fiesta inequalities. At the terminal scale the section price
  includes the physical grade dilation and coefficient of core(tau_N(v));
  core deletion decreases the coefficient norm. The bank pays the resulting
  weighted response. The pitch is nu_i below the terminal scale and nu_N-3 at
  the terminal scale, so the next-step threshold nu_{i+1}-4 is admissible.
  The stated response/exponential smallness conditions and the earlier
  local-transfer theorem give the downward served induction, conditional on
  the specified exact profile and finite-menu inputs.

  The width bill uses the actual hatted-coupling factor, accumulated columns
  and factorial order. Affine hatted coupling and the previously proved
  column subpower estimate make the logarithmic width bill negligible against
  scale. The opened-depth treasury payment bounds both the vacuum term and
  the scale gap; a strict exponent margin gives the requested mesh power.
  Finitely many remaining depths are absorbed into one finite constant.
  Common bounded-grade-label and interiority hypotheses retain the source
  quantifier order, including a volume tail uniform over every period, label
  and site.

  Relevant inspected correspondence includes Work/I01 and Corona/{Fill,Fit}
  for the final cover correction, I04/Baskets/Gardens for width and roots,
  Paddle/Velvet/ChaletS/SpringT for the scale/terminal interfaces,
  Accent/Newell/Arbol/Glacier for finite census and normalization, and the
  earlier inspected public FullVolume/Hearth/Gist route. These source paths
  support the displayed consumer proof; named forwarded receipts are not
  counted as proofs of their upstream production. No builds, source edits or
  metadata approvals were made.

  <section|Whole-gas absorption of localized
  logarithms><label|whole-gas-absorption-of-localized-logarithms>

  Reviewed parent soft-log-fusion.tex at SHA-256
  <verbatim|a8caa20893e55269853ba6e26d08b60c6f09b3f3572a00c7e7aff8d20f5c43db>
  against the full Mallow/Passage and Kitchen proofs. No remaining
  substantive local mathematical or main-step correspondence defect was found
  after explicitly requiring real-valued factors and measurable,
  gauge-invariant, final-flag-local hard factors and eligibility predicates.

  The Mayer expansion is absolutely summable. Every nonzero soft factor meets
  a flag, and exact hard inventory coverage attaches it to a hard
  constituent. Thus there are no nonzero purely soft components.
  Connected-component decomposition and flattening are inverse on nonzero
  terms; pairwise disjoint total supports prevent label duplication, and
  exact local flag equality plus all original eligibility tests are
  preserved. This proves the actual gas times exp(sum logs) identity and
  transports absolute convergence to the new gas. The empty-flag case is
  included.

  With a fixed logarithmic correction and a tilted hard family, joint
  witnesses pay products without an extra constituent count. Inflating hard
  prices by exp(kappa), bounding soft Mayer factors by twice their logarithm
  prices, and retaining at least one hard constituent leave exp(-kappa). The
  previous distinct-set forest bound with reserve one gives
  exp(-kappa)(exp(Gamma)-1) at the original support exponent. Anchor
  dependence, debt D, locality, measurability and eligibility persist. Two
  applications supply the exact two fusion identities, conditional on the
  actual correction fields satisfying the displayed flag, site-price and
  smallness hypotheses. Their analytic construction and payment remain open
  upstream.

  Also inspected the revised dependency paragraph in leaf-expansion.tex at
  SHA-256 <verbatim|d6ba28b61050f42f1826c1bc223f24beb480b2cbf74f0eb230945b1835f1adec>.
  Its cross-references correctly discharge the combinatorial cluster/mixed
  estimates and whole-gas fusion under their precise hypotheses; the earlier
  local differentiation pass is retained. No builds, source edits or metadata
  approvals were made.

