  Lean proofs. Existing local chapter passes remain conditional on their
  stated inputs. Excludes the team's current packet/action,
  stationary-horizon and selected centered-service production work.

  <\enumerate>
    <item><strong|Actual full-mesh bounds and Cauchy comparison.> The generic
    theorem in smooth-limits does not prove its hypotheses. Exact source
    endpoints are YM.FullVolume.genuine (FullVolume/Literal.lean),
    YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Legato.Campaign.purchased and .realUV
    (FullVolume/Fields/Filled.lean). The substantive bridges are Run.financed
    in Literal, paying every hopped derivative word using prepared rows and
    corrected detectors, and Bandage.Rising.cinema in
    FullVolume/Fields/Seat.lean, comparing different ultraviolet cutoffs on a
    common history at a fixed reference level. Prove the uniform
    all-mixed-difference budgets, then actual dense Cauchy estimates with
    quantifiers independent of the later cutoff; extend to Cyclic using the
    previously proved regularity argument. Merely selecting another
    subsequence cannot meet the public full-mesh conclusion. This is the
    cleanest next bounded package once centered estimates are available.

    <item><strong|Actual phase inputs, especially all-copy slabs and
    real-grid approximation.> YM.Next.Phase.replicas and .seats
    (Next/PHASE/Seats.lean) supply Bench from CellHyp via Roots.cutoff_bound,
    Passage.point_bound and Trains.travel_price. Their key quantifier is a
    slab subwidth chosen before the arbitrary exterior word, with an
    exponential repeated-word bound uniform in replica count. The existing
    abstract bounded-slab and compression arguments do not prove this.
    Separately YM.Org.Grill (Org/Input.lean) needs arbitrarily fine cofinal
    real grid approximants with joint all-copy error control, not positivity
    or CellHyp alone. YM.Next.UVStress.provides_Grill
    (Next/UV_STRESS/Grill.lean) reduces this to Furnace and proves the
    old/new conditional-product and basis-linear-combination handoff;
    Next/BOUNDARY/Synchronize.grid_count supplies the common-refinement
    consumer. The actual old/new all-copy approximation estimate must still
    be supplied, not inferred from that consumer. Finish the detector Funds
    producer for the same corrected trials before invoking
    YM.Next.Phase.material and .rows (Next/PHASE/Assembly.lean);
    Org.Phase.Loom.cleanse uses this to preserve the null ideal for every
    character. These are necessary for faithful fields and O(4), not optional
    phase refinements.

    <item><strong|Actual calibrated stress/Ward comparison along every
    vanishing scale sequence.> The trace-asymptotic chapter proves the scalar
    asymptotic from explicit comparison inputs. Its actual supplier is
    YM.Trace.Over.gang (TraceExtension/Chart/Line.lean), producing Gallery,
    through Litpay, pays_sky, gravity and Store_l. Gallery requires a strict
    subsequence of every positive sequence tending to zero, on the same
    selected hierarchy. The central local obligation is YM.Trace.Over.reveals
    (Chart/Masts.lean): rank-one conserved-current kernel and a moving
    conserved tensor whose physical normalized limit is materialB and whose
    scaled trace tends to 4 forceR times OScale. The proof uses three
    calibrated Rod directions, rungs/formulate, the actual Ward identities,
    serene/yields/blossoms and finite-dimensional rank comparison; abstract
    rank or a freely chosen stress tensor is insufficient. Chart/Time.Store_l
    then transfers this to Scribe, and Trace.crest_ready (Belfry.lean) and
    Trace.Target.assembled (Endpoint.lean) finish the already translated
    measure/asymptotic consumers. Need prove the actual Ward/calibration and
    all-bad-sequence scaling suppliers, rather than restating Gallery as an
    input.
  </enumerate>

