  <section|Kernel itinerary jet closure audit><label|kernel-itinerary-jet-closure-audit>

  Bounded read-only audit against pinned source
  3456e5e75cf8d4cd558955a5c7638fba2d68f464. Read integration
  normalization-jets/local-covariance and E6 Pedi, StampCost, Trail, Tax,
  Export, Cascades, Gust, Moraine, StreamsCost and Corbel. Existing finite
  inverse-jet, principal-window counting and far-error proofs already supply
  the content needed for YM.ConnectedActivityE6.Blaze.Foramen.debris. No new
  inverse-entry jet hypothesis should be introduced. The names are
  Foramen.debris in Gust, Vine.glacierA/glacierS in Cascades, and
  Silica.Clutch.slopeLedger in Moraine (not Tablet or Maraine).

  The remaining substantive manuscript bridge is the individual itinerary
  expansion and rooted price calculation. Pedi.canon/plurality bounds finite
  matrix words, sums the colour indices, and integrates the glide parameter
  on a common neighborhood. With c colours and correction order n, the
  determinant word (A-1)P_s(-E_s)^(n+1) has n+3 factors, cap amplitude
  c^4(a+1)ht and ratio ct; the symmetric correction D(-sD)^n has n+1 factors,
  amplitude c^2 w and ratio cw. Their derivative scales are the respective
  word lengths times the common factor scale. The quadratic word (-D)^(n+1)A
  has n+2 factors; two endpoint colour sums and protected Gaussian coordinate
  bounds p give amplitude p^2 c^4 a w and ratio cw. Nonhot endpoint and
  locally zero cutoff cases must first give zero germs; unarmed paths vanish
  by the 3B finite-range property. The source endpoint bound is
  Moraine.occupancy; it cannot be replaced by a bound on arbitrary Gaussian
  coordinates.

  Tax.scalar/Export.out provide an essential volume-uniform rooted sum, which
  is stronger than convergence in operator norm. At halo m\<gtr\>=4, let
  K=ballCost(3B+2)<em|L^4>\|Axis\|. Armed n+u paths from one initial bond
  number at most K^(n+u). A visited fixed root restricts that initial bond to
  radius (n+u+1)(mB+1), giving at most ballCost((u+1)(mB+1))<em|16^n>L^4*\|Axis\|
  choices. The support cover is at most (n+u+1)<em|steady(m). Thus the
  weighted root sum is bounded by H>C times the geometric series of ratio
  Q<em|16>K<em|exp(A>steady(m)+2 epsilon), where
  H=ballCost((u+1)(mB+1))<em|L^4>\|Axis\|<em|K^u>exp(A(u+1)steady(m)). Ratio
  at most 1/2 gives 2HC. StreamsCost.fluid first absorbs the derivative
  length factor by replacing C by C*[1+(1+u)d]^j and Q by Q*2^j. Negative
  upper exponent of Q beats the subpower geometric count, while H preserves
  C's exponent. This is the precise missing mathematical content between the
  existing chapters and StreamsCost.enlighten/Corbel.waits. Sent the formulas
  and source locations to parent; no manuscript edits.

