  <section|Deterministic safety producer \V bounded source
  audit><label|deterministic-safety-producer--bounded-source-audit>

  Inspected E6/Peak.lean, PatchCap.lean, MinBranches.lean and the immediate
  Issue/IssuePlan/StampQ/Batch interfaces at the same source pin. Exact
  producer: <verbatim|YM.ConnectedActivityE6.Target.issue> builds
  <verbatim|GrantBodies.safety> using <verbatim|Coat.scopes>,
  <verbatim|Coat.tends_val>, and <verbatim|Coat.ready>; <verbatim|circulates>
  packages Cash, and <verbatim|Target.quotesTogether>/<verbatim|Planning.waits>
  supply the selected common delayed run. This is a genuine deterministic
  field estimate, not merely a choice of a positive scalar.

  For q colour coordinates and s=Coat.scale, choose xi=min((q+1)^(-1),
  tau/(3q s^(-1)\|Y\|+1)). At a clean site, writing C for the actual
  nonlinear bill and R(v) for the real response, the exact three errors are
  \|\|C-R(v)\|\|\<less\>=H, \|\|R(v)-R(mu)\|\|\<less\>=q s^(-1)Y xi t, and
  \|\|R(mu)\|\|\<less\>=E. <verbatim|SliceRows.strokes> gives H of rate -1;
  <verbatim|Coat.hips> gives the middle bound; <verbatim|pressure_mean> gives
  E of rate -1. <verbatim|tiny_flame> pays H,E each by tau t/3. Thus
  bill\<less\>=tau t. The pre-L guide maximum A supplies fine entry
  \<less\>=(A/L^2+tau)t and predictor entry \<less\>=(A+tau)t.
  <verbatim|Work.E05.curvature_lower>, after <verbatim|marks_here> supplies
  the small-chord region, converts these into fine toll\<less\>t/4 and
  predictor wire\<less\>Wt.

  Choice order: pre-L A; tau=sqrt(direct)/32; sufficiently large L; then
  W\<gtr\>2(A+tau)/sqrt(penalty); shell and rotation constants and uniform
  mean cap C; a=max(C+1,gamma K); xi; finally a common delayed x threshold.
  Reduced margin xi/2 gives strict field plateau below a t.

  Substantive missing sublemma beyond the already translated finite-step
  predictor IFT is <verbatim|YM.ConnectedActivityE6.Forward.approves> in
  MinBranches. It proves a torus-uniform plateau for every tag: strict branch
  neighborhoods at the cover identity, continuous frames/decks/best, finite
  tags, a finite-coordinate product neighborhood, and a route-length halo
  imply both normalized tag likelihoods exactly one.
  <verbatim|SliceRows.marks_here> combines this with the common local gauge
  and W(x)\<less\>=min(r,delta/4), B\<gtr\>=2d+12; it also supplies small
  plaquette and mismatch chords before curvature comparison. Parent informed
  with exact formulas and ordering. Read-only audit, no source or manuscript
  changes.

