  <section|Elementary projection closure \V corrected
  pass><label|elementary-projection-closure--corrected-pass>

  Parent <verbatim|projection-payment-producer.tex> final fingerprint
  <verbatim|5637b0d8aa15de99a7153a5778f54b2054ba92688c318a017dfd244d4a2c8e83>
  receives a bounded mathematical/source pass, conditional on the identified
  common sector/path inputs. Read the full initial manuscript and the
  corrected payment subsection. Immediate sources inspected in full include
  <verbatim|MergeProof/North/{Partly,Shawl,Morsel,Tibetan,Freckles}.lean>,
  <verbatim|Blush/Little.lean>, <verbatim|Graces/Aspire.lean>, and
  <verbatim|Push/LOCAL_SPLITTING/Funding.lean>, in addition to the
  coefficient-array sources listed above.

  The initial manuscript still deferred the two small bills to their eventual
  payment without proving it. The final version repairs that gap with the
  actual outgoing forced allowance. Set P=exp((loglog x)^2), P_f=P(beta_f),
  kappa=exp(-P^(1/5)/2), and s=2exp(-mu P_f^2/16). Eventually P\<less\>=P_f
  and kappa^{-1}s\<less\>=2exp(-mu P_f^2/32), which has every negative upper
  exponent. This pays the normalized forced price even after multiplication
  by the inverse gain and the fixed L^d. The tail price has the independent
  negative exponent q/4. Both bounds are multiplied by the nonnegative mass
  reserve at most m, without dividing by m. The logarithm of hitWidth*kappa
  tends to minus infinity, since hitWidth=(2B+1)^4. This is the content
  needed from <verbatim|Blush.efferv/fruition> and <verbatim|Graces.compass>.

  The principal single-cluster bound follows by retaining one rooted
  nonnegative summand and using the already purchased t/(1-gamma)\<less\>=1.
  The polynomial reserve proves its actual mass bound, including absence of a
  principal regular term for flagged input. The output coefficient-profile
  identity is established entrywise via the actual pupil derivative/door, and
  then through the splitting hook. The large projection allowance follows
  from finite power growth being dominated by exp(sqrt(beta_f)); the
  Salt.scent formula retains its three separate (1+N) factors and the
  pre-length Release floor is selected in the correct order. This removes
  these stated elementary projection payment boundaries, but is not a proof
  of the remaining upstream Gaussian/path inputs.

