  Refract, Magnitude, Racers, Silt, Frenzy, Scenes and Faint; bounded Batch,
  Steps.cross_seed and Climb.Cells.Colors. No build run. The candidate does
  not yet prove its unconditional uniform external detector/classifier.

  <\itemize-minus>
    <item>Hidden.matrix_meal constructs a matrix of polynomial entries
    bit(q_c,i), whose determinant is shown nonzero by evaluation on a Taylor
    tower with one nonzero sheet at each distinct order. It is not a
    numerical invertible matrix obtained by a dual-basis choice. The exact
    adjugate/domain cancellation and all-displacement/all-upper-probe span of
    group_meal must replace that paragraph.

    <item>Rumbles.cluster_clear is not an ordinary radial collision limit.
    Double hits on the distinguished insertion can be more singular.
    Frenzy.duet_path assigns their product poles to Silt; Deep.clear peels
    the finite homogeneous expansion and Faint.clears_faint separates the
    harmonic pole from terms cleared by r-2 radial powers. The draft omits
    this substantive argument. Required output is the actual circulation
    nullity at the same external capacity, with r=4+k+j and M\<gtr\>8+k+l+2j,
    then the weighted induction. Otherwise the detector must remain
    conditional.

    <item>Quiet-charge statement omits the Colors filtration A_a(V_k) subset
    V_(k+1), all k\<less\>=d. Racers.motor_low uses it at k=4 before
    opposite-reflection parity. Signed covariance/reality/unit alone do not
    provide that premise.

    <item>The panel is D_p:Sheet0 to Flavor1; X is an arbitrary uncoloured
    sheet, not a colour coordinate. One-to-zero kernels separate only when
    all nonzero displacement tests are used; fixed-position nondegeneracy is
    false in these unequal dimensions. The triangular residue must include
    point_fares realization of X, common factor 4 dim(g), opposite near sign
    and zero far-mark limit. Real mixed-product injectivity and polarization
    need explicit explanation or a precise canonical proof reference.

    <item>Stabilizer near relation is divergence/free_shift, not Bianchi.
    Reflection parity selects three candidate vectors; the separate swap
    projection reduces their span. The cross-seed value is -2 normal, not an
    unexplained nonzero scalar. Far relation is Bianchi with the displayed
    signs.

    <item>Actual Scene tests use a line axis transverse to the component
    being tested and all configuration derivatives of the Ward sum. The
    strict-order segment construction otherwise checks. The final finite
    real-dimensional kernel selection and Euler/opposite-parity step are
    sound once their corrected inputs are supplied.

    <item>In the coalescence proof, surplus distinguished legs vanish
    identically and lower-length components are absent before taking any
    limit, so divergent spectator contractions never occur. State this
    counting explicitly; the bounded-jet invariant generation argument is
    otherwise sound with independent polynomial coordinates, invariant p and
    natural grade indices stated.
  </itemize-minus>

